        <TryIt />
        <details class="reveal"><summary>Show one possible answer</summary><div class="flow">
          <pre class="code"><code set:html={hiN(taskAns)} /></pre>
          <p>Output: <code>10 30 40</code>, <code>10 30 40</code>, <code>10 30</code>, <code>30</code>. The loop stops before <code>size - 1</code> because each step reads the next slot, <code>arr[i + 1]</code>, the same as the deletion code in Part 4. Removing 99 changes nothing, since it is not there. Removing the last value (40) shifts nothing: only the size drops. You will write a method like <code>indexOf</code> yourself in the <a href={base + '/itc120/searching/'}>Searching</a> lesson (linear search).</p>
        </div></details>
