      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Four operations: access, traversal, insertion, deletion.</li>
          <li>Arrays give direct access when you know the index: one step.</li>
          <li>Inserting in the middle shifts later values right (start from the end). Deleting shifts them left.</li>
          <li>As data grows, repeated shifting means more work for the program.</li>
          <li>Arrays and linked lists have different trade-offs. The better choice depends on the operation.</li>
        </ol>
